## Exploring

A question about the code or other files that would cost you more reading
than its answer is worth goes to an explorer: `ccc run explorer`. Its prompt
holds a few related questions, the directory to read, and the absolute path
of the report it writes. It answers with citations and prescribes nothing;
its report is a claim, so check the cited lines your work rests on. Small
lookups you do yourself.

{{ explorer_rules("report, at a new path named after your task
(`exploration-<task>-<N>.md`) in the directory your prompt gives for what you
write, or in a new `mktemp -d` directory when it gives none") }}

Your failure route for a launch is your reply: finish without the explorer's
answer if you can and say what is missing, otherwise `ESCALATE`.

